# dsh-update runtime state and fetched installs -- never commit.
#
# WHY A NESTED .gitignore RATHER THAN LINES IN THE REPO ROOT
# These two directories are large and machine-local, and the reason each is ignored is specific to
# this subsystem, so the statement belongs next to the thing it describes.
#
#   state/   pin, baseline, per-candidate analysis, the append-only history, engine logs, and -- for
#            any verify run that booted an engine -- a COPIED .credentials.yaml inside
#            state/candidates/<ver>/home/. That copy is already excluded by the repo-root
#            `.credentials.yaml` pattern (verified with `git check-ignore`: matches at any depth),
#            but it must not rely on that alone: `state/` is ignored wholesale so a secret can never
#            enter git through a path nobody thought about. `verify.mjs` should stop copying it and
#            pass the key through the child environment instead -- see SPEC.md section C14. Until
#            then, this file is the mitigation.
#
#   vendor/  a real `npm install` of a candidate, ~215 MB and 25,000 files for one version. It is
#            reproducible from `fetch <version>` and must never be committed.
#
# The pipeline's SOURCE (SPEC.md, README.md, bin/, lib/, tests/) is deliberately NOT ignored: it is
# the part that must reach every machine.
state/
vendor/
